---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { contacts, mailto } from '../config/site';

// Update both dates whenever the policy text changes.
const effective = 'October 19, 2026';
const updated = 'October 19, 2026';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy policy"
  description="How Math Dragons handles information: the app collects no data, has no ads and no accounts. This policy also covers playmathdragons.com."
  path="/privacy"
>
  <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
  <p class="muted">Effective {effective}. Last updated {updated}.</p>

  <p>
    This policy explains how {contacts.developer} ("we", "us") handles information in the Math
    Dragons app ("the app") and on this website, playmathdragons.com ("the website"). The short
    version: <strong>the app collects no data.</strong> It has no ads, no accounts, and it doesn't
    send anything anywhere.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    Math Dragons is made by {contacts.developer}. For privacy questions, email
    <a href={mailto(contacts.privacy, 'Math Dragons privacy')}>{contacts.privacy}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>2. The app</h2>

  <h3>What the app stores, and where</h3>
  <p>
    To run the game, the app keeps this information <strong>only on your device</strong>, in the
    app's private storage:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>the dragon's name (chosen in the app) and its growth stage</li>
    <li>game progress: scores, levels, stars, scales earned, play time, achievements and streaks</li>
    <li>which math facts have been practiced, how often they were answered correctly, and how long answers took</li>
    <li>when the game was played (dates and times of play)</li>
    <li>cosmetics owned and equipped, and settings such as sound and music</li>
    <li>a note that the app was installed during the beta, so beta families can get the full unlock free at launch</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    The app never sends this information to us or anyone else, and we can't see it. The operating
    system keeps it in the app's private storage, where other apps can't read it.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Device backups:</strong> if your device's own backup is turned on (iCloud Backup on
    iPhone or iPad, or Google's backup on Android), it may include the app's data, the same as other
    apps. That backup is stored in your Apple or Google account under their privacy policies. We
    can't see it.
  </p>

  <h3>What the app does not collect</h3>
  <p>The app does not collect, store or send:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>names, email addresses, or any other information that identifies a person</li>
    <li>location</li>
    <li>device identifiers or advertising IDs</li>
    <li>analytics, usage tracking or telemetry</li>
    <li>photos, contacts or any other data from the device</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    The app contains no advertising, no analytics tools and no third-party services that collect
    data. It doesn't ask for an account and works without an internet connection.
  </p>

  <h3>Links out of the app</h3>
  <p>
    The only links in the app are in Settings, under <strong>For Parents</strong>: this privacy
    policy, a feedback page and a help page on playmathdragons.com. Each one is behind a grown-ups
    check (a multiplication problem young children can't easily solve) and opens in your web
    browser. The app has no social features and no other links.
  </p>

  <h3>Purchases</h3>
  <p>
    The app has no in-app purchases right now. Everything is free during the beta. If we add paid
    features later, we'll update this policy before they launch, and any purchase will go through
    the App Store or Google Play behind a grown-ups check.
  </p>

  <h3>Beta testing through Apple and Google</h3>
  <p>
    If you join the beta, Apple (TestFlight) or Google (Google Play testing) handles the download.
    They may share limited information with us under their own privacy policies, such as how many
    people installed the app, crash reports, and any feedback or screenshots you choose to send
    through TestFlight. For the Android beta, you join a Google Group, so Google shows us (the group
    owner) the email address you joined with. Other testers can't see it. We use it only to run the
    beta, and we remove the group when the beta ends, or remove you sooner if you ask.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Children's privacy</h2>
  <p>
    Math Dragons is made for children ages 5 to 12. The app does not collect personal information
    from anyone, including children under 13, and it never asks a child to enter any. There is no
    chat, no sharing, and no way for a child to contact anyone through the app.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you're a parent or guardian with a question or concern, email
    <a href={mailto(contacts.privacy, 'Math Dragons privacy')}>{contacts.privacy}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>4. The website</h2>
  <p>
    This website has no ads, no analytics, no cookies and no forms. It is hosted by Cloudflare,
    which, like any web host, processes basic technical information (such as your IP address and
    browser type) to deliver pages and protect the site from abuse. We don't use that information
    to identify or track you.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you email us, we use your email address and message only to reply and to fix problems you
    report. Our email is handled by Microsoft 365. We delete support emails within 12 months after
    the conversation ends, or sooner if you ask.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Do Not Track:</strong> we don't track visitors on this website or across other
    websites, so there is nothing for Do Not Track or Global Privacy Control signals to turn off.
    If we ever add analytics, we will update this policy first and respect those signals.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Sharing</h2>
  <p>
    We don't sell or share personal information. The app has nothing to share, because it doesn't
    collect any.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Deleting data</h2>
  <p>Because the app's data lives on your device, you control it:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>iPhone or iPad:</strong> delete the app to remove all of its data.</li>
    <li>
      <strong>Android:</strong> open Settings, then Apps, then Math Dragons, then Storage (or
      Storage &amp; cache), and tap Clear storage (Clear data on some phones). Or uninstall the app.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    A copy may remain in your own device backup until that backup is replaced or deleted in your
    Apple or Google account settings.
  </p>
  <p>
    There is no data on our servers to delete. To have us delete an email you sent, write to
    <a href={mailto(contacts.privacy, 'Delete my email')}>{contacts.privacy}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    If this policy changes, we'll update the date at the top. If we change how the app handles
    information, we'll update this page before the change reaches the app.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    {contacts.developer}<br />
    Privacy: <a href={mailto(contacts.privacy, 'Math Dragons privacy')}>{contacts.privacy}</a><br />
    Support: <a href={mailto(contacts.support, 'Math Dragons')}>{contacts.support}</a>
  </p>
</Base>
